# The repository is the stack: six packages, their configs and launch files,
# and nothing else. Everything that produced the stack rather than being it --
# working notes, the measurement harness, the simulator scaffolding, and
# anything a build or a run writes -- stays on disk and out of the history.

# Build and run outputs.
build/
install/
log/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Working notes. Written to think with, not to ship.
docs/

# The measurement harness: benchmarks, parameter sweeps, scoring runs and
# everything they leave behind. Correctness is covered by the packages' own
# tests; these exist to answer questions that are already answered.
tools/

# Simulator scaffolding: the CARLA bridge, the recording scripts and the
# sensor mappings. The CARLA-side nodes that the stack itself needs are in
# src/monoscale_carla; this is the rig that drives them.
sim/

# Except the conditions the bags were recorded under, which are not scaffolding.
# `sensor_kit_calibration.yaml` is where vision_fisheye.param.yaml's mount
# heights and rotations come from -- when that file moved a millimetre on
# 2026-09-11 the odometry's extrinsics had to move with it, and they cannot move
# in one commit if half the pair is untracked. The sensor mapping is the kit the
# bench recorded with, and the four scripts are the recipe that made the bags.
# `test_sim_copy_matches_live.py` holds these against the live tree.
!sim/
!sim/README.md
!sim/*.sh
!sim/*.py
!sim/ioniq_carla_bridge/
!sim/ioniq_carla_bridge/config/
!sim/ioniq_carla_bridge/config/*.yaml
sim/logs/
sim/**/*.bak
sim/**/*.before-*

# Recordings and grids.
*.db3
*.npz
*.bag
